{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"notification-center","name":"Notification Center","version":"0.1.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":[],"author":"mclaudiopt","description":"Queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners through a small companion web app. Talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Notifications"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Notification Center\n\n> **This Shard does nothing on its own: it needs the companion app on the TV.** The app (an unsigned `.wgt`, id `NotifCtr01.NotifCenter`, with a\n> background service `NotifCtr01.Svc`) is not part of the catalog. Get it from https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center/releases, sign it\n> with your own certificate and install it (see \"Install the companion app\" below). Without it, `notify` queues messages but nothing is shown.\n\nAny device on your LAN (PC, phone, script) can `POST` a message to this Shard. By default the TV shows it as a **native Samsung banner**\n(top-right, with the OK / \"View history\" buttons, kept in the TV's own notification history) **on top of whatever is running, without opening\nany app**: the companion app's background service posts it. Optionally the message can also (or only) be shown as a **full-screen card**, which\ndoes bring the companion app to the foreground for a few seconds. Everything runs on the TV, no PC is needed afterwards.\n\n> **Status: early.** It works end to end on one TV (see \"Tested on\"). Read \"Limitations\" before installing.\n\nThe panel (tab **Notifications**) and the app screen are bilingual (English by default, Portuguese optional: use the EN/PT switch in the panel, or `POST .../api/lang` with `{\"lang\":\"pt\"}`) and use a One UI style look. The banner itself is always the TV's own native one.\n\n## Permissions\n\nNone. It does not use `exec`.\n\n## Network\n\n- **Incoming:** HTTP routes under `/plugins/notification-center/api/` (`notify`, `notifications`, `recent`, `lang`, `ui`, `nt.js`),\n  open to every device that can reach Vetro, like the rest of Vetro when pairing is off.\n- **Outgoing:** one call, to Vetro itself on `127.0.0.1:8099` (`POST /apps/launch`, body `{\"appId\": \"...\"}`), to start the companion app or its service.\n  The app is launched at most once every 10 seconds. It talks to no other host and downloads no code.\n- The companion app's service reads this Shard on the TV's own LAN address, port 8099 (`GET notifications`). Nothing leaves the TV.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nOnly the display language (`lang`, `en` or `pt`) is kept in `ctx.config`. The id of the companion app is fixed in the code (`NotifCtr01.NotifCenter`), so no route can point the Shard at another app.\nThe queue (up to 5 active notifications) and the list of the last 20 sent are kept in memory only and are cleared when the Shard stops.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nmode \"banner\" (default, native banner over the running app, no app switch):\nany device --POST notify--> Shard (queue) --POST /apps/launch--> Vetro starts the app's background SERVICE (headless)\nservice --GET notifications--> Shard --> webapis.postPlainNotification(title, message, seconds) --> TV banner + notification history\n\nmodes \"full\" / \"both\" (full-screen card; the companion app comes to the foreground):\nany device --POST notify--> Shard (queue) --POST /apps/launch--> Vetro launches the companion app\napp --GET notifications--> Shard --> card on screen (+ new Notification(...) native banner for \"both\") --> exits after `duration`\n```\n\nThe full-screen app is a **thin loader**: its logic is `nt.js`, served by this Shard, so you can change it from the Vetro panel without\nreinstalling the app. The background service is self-contained (it downloads no code).\n\n## Install\n\n1. Vetro with root connected. If Vetro keeps restarting, set the TV's **Host PC IP to `127.0.0.1`** (Developer Mode); otherwise\n   it can end up in safe mode (\"Resume plugins\", then restart Vetro).\n2. Install this Shard from the catalog and switch it on.\n3. Build and install the companion app (below) with your own certificate. It needs the privileges `notification` and `internet`.\n4. Send a notification:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"seconds\":30}'\n```\n\n**With pairing on (Vetro's default)** a request from another device goes through Vetro's sign-in like every other route, so a script on the LAN needs\n`Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Pair the script once (the TV shows a 6-digit code), as described in Vetro's `SIGN-IN.md`:\n\n```\ncurl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"scripts\"}' http://<TV-IP>:8099/auth/pair\ncurl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"id\":\"<id>\",\"code\":\"<code>\"}' http://<TV-IP>:8099/auth/confirm   # returns the token\ncurl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\"}'\n```\n\nThe companion app on the TV itself (127.0.0.1) needs no key. With pairing off (Vetro's \"Disable pairing mode\") any device on the LAN can send notifications.\n\nFields: `message` (required, 200 characters), `title` (40), `level` (`info`, `ok`, `warn`, `alert`; colours the card on the app screen and the panel, default `info`), `duration` (1-60, default 8: seconds the notification stays on the TV screen before the app returns to the previous one; very short values may cut the native banner short), `mode` (`both` default, `banner` = native Samsung banner only, `full` = full-screen card only), `seconds` (5-300, how long it waits in the queue), `open`\n(`false` only queues it, without launching the app). The page of this Shard (tab **Notifications**) has a form for it.\n\n## Install the companion app (required)\n\nDownload the unsigned `.wgt` from the releases of https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center, or build it from the four files below (also in `app/`) plus any 512x512 `icon.png`.\nSign it with your own certificate and install it with Apps2Samsung, TV-Store or Tizen Studio. The app id must stay `NotifCtr01.NotifCenter` and the service id `NotifCtr01.Svc`.\n\n### Source (copy these four files)\n\n`config.xml`\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<widget xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets\" xmlns:tizen=\"http://tizen.org/ns/widgets\" id=\"http://localhost/notifcenter\" version=\"0.2.0\" viewmodes=\"maximized\">\n  <tizen:application id=\"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" package=\"NotifCtr01\" required_version=\"6.0\"/>\n  <name>Notification Center</name>\n  <icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n  <content src=\"index.html\"/>\n  <access origin=\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\" subdomains=\"false\"/>\n  <feature name=\"http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/internet\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/notification\"/>\n  <tizen:profile name=\"tv-samsung\"/>\n  <tizen:service id=\"NotifCtr01.Svc\" auto-restart=\"false\" on-boot=\"false\">\n    <tizen:content src=\"service.js\"/>\n    <tizen:name>Notification Center service</tizen:name>\n    <tizen:icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n    <tizen:description>Shows the Samsung notification banner without opening an app</tizen:description>\n  </tizen:service>\n</widget>\n```\n\n`index.html`\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Notification Center</title></head>\n<body style=\"background:#0f1218;color:#e8ecf2;font:28px sans-serif;margin:40px\">\n<div id=\"log\"></div>\n<script src=\"js/app.js\"></script>\n</body></html>\n```\n\n`js/app.js` (the loader)\n\n```js\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASES = [\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\"];\n  var PATH = \"/plugins/notification-center/api/nt.js\";\n  var logEl = document.getElementById(\"log\"), i = 0;\n  function say(t) { var d = document.createElement(\"div\"); d.textContent = t; logEl.appendChild(d); }\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= BASES.length) { say(\"Could not load nt.js from the Shard. Is it running?\"); return; }\n    var s = document.createElement(\"script\");\n    s.src = BASES[i++] + PATH + \"?t=\" + new Date().getTime();\n    s.onerror = function () { say(\"nt.js failed: \" + s.src.split(\"?\")[0]); next(); };\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  })();\n})();\n```\n\n`service.js` (the background service)\n\n```js\n// Background service of the Notification Center companion app (Node.js in the TV's web service runtime).\n// Vetro starts it (POST /apps/launch) each time a notification is queued in \"banner\" mode; it reads the Shard's queue and posts the native\n// Samsung banner with webapis.postPlainNotification, without opening any app.\n// The Shard is reached on the TV's own LAN address (found here), because loopback is not reachable from the service on every TV.\nvar HOSTS = ['127.0.0.1'];\ntry {\n  var ifs = require('os').networkInterfaces();\n  Object.keys(ifs).forEach(function (k) { ifs[k].forEach(function (i) { if (i.family === 'IPv4' && !i.internal && HOSTS.indexOf(i.address) < 0) { HOSTS.push(i.address); } }); });\n} catch (e) { /* keep loopback only */ }\nvar PATH = '/plugins/notification-center/api/notifications';\nvar seen = {};\nfunction check() {\n  var i = 0;\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= HOSTS.length) { return; }\n    fetch('http://' + HOSTS[i++] + ':8099' + PATH + '?t=' + Date.now()).then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error('http ' + r.status); } return r.json(); }).then(function (d) {\n      (d.notifications || []).forEach(function (n) {\n        if (seen[n.id]) { return; }\n        seen[n.id] = 1;\n        if (n.mode !== 'banner') { return; }   // \"full\" and \"both\" are shown by the companion app screen\n        try { webapis.postPlainNotification(n.title || 'Notification', n.message || '', parseInt(n.duration, 10) || 8); } catch (e) { /* API not available */ }\n      });\n    }).catch(function () { next(); });\n  })();\n}\nmodule.exports.onStart = check;\nmodule.exports.onRequest = check;\nmodule.exports.onStop = function () {};\n```\n\nThese files are also in the `app/` folder next to this README. A ready-made, **unsigned** `.wgt` (with an icon) is attached to\nthe releases of https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center (a catalog Shard can only hold text files, so the `.wgt` and its icon are not here).\nAdd any 512x512 `icon.png`, zip the files as `.wgt`, sign it and install it (Apps2Samsung, TV-Store, Tizen Studio).\n`nt.js` also tries the address it was loaded from. If the app shows \"nt.js failed\" (loopback does not answer on some TVs), build the app with the TV's LAN address too:\nadd the TV's own LAN address to `BASES` in `js/app.js` and `nt.js`, and a matching `<access origin=\"...\">` to `config.xml`.\n\n## Limitations (all measured on a real TV)\n\n- **Banner mode** uses Samsung's `webapis.postPlainNotification(title, message, seconds)`, which exists only inside a web *service* (a background\n  `<tizen:service>` of the app, Node.js 18 in `wrt-service-launcher`). It takes plain text and a duration: **no icon, level or colour** on the native\n  banner (the level only colours the panel and the full-screen card).\n- **Full-screen card / both**: the web `Notification` API only works while the web app is on screen, so the companion app comes to the front, shows\n  the card for `duration` seconds and exits; what was playing is interrupted briefly. `tizen.notification` does not exist in the app (UI) context.\n- The service reaches the Shard through the TV's own LAN address (loopback is not reachable from the service on the TV I tested, `EHOSTUNREACH`).\n- Plain `notification_test`, `libnotification` sockets, D-Bus and writing the notification database were all dead ends (see the repository's `docs/NATIVE-NOTIFICATIONS.md`).\n- The TV refuses to run **unsigned script files** (\"the file is NOT signed\"); inline commands through Vetro still work. This Shard needs neither.\n- Whether the previous screen comes back cleanly after the app exits was tested only from the launcher, not yet over\n  every kind of source (live TV, HDMI).\n- With pairing off, any device that can reach Vetro's port can send notifications and make Vetro launch the companion app (at most once every 10 s); with pairing on, senders need a key (see above).\n\n## Tested on\n\nSamsung Q70C (TQ55Q70CATXXC), Tizen 9.0, Vetro 0.6.9, Shard 0.1.0 installed from the bundle as a file (Developer mode), with the companion\napp `NotifCtr01.NotifCenter` 0.1.0 installed on the TV.\n\n**Pairing off (Vetro's \"Disable pairing mode\" on): tested on the TV.** Notifications sent with `curl` from a PC on the LAN: native banner top-right\n(`mode: banner`), full-screen card (`mode: full`) and both (`mode: both`); English and Portuguese (`lang`); the four levels (`info`, `ok`, `warn`,\n`alert`) with their icons; `duration` (a 3 s card stayed 3 s); Resend from \"Recently sent\" in the panel; the app's loader falling back to the\naddress nt.js was loaded from. The TV returned to the previous app after each notification.\n\n**Pairing on: NOT tested on a TV.** The Bearer-token flow above is the one documented in Vetro's `SIGN-IN.md` (`/auth/pair`, `/auth/confirm`,\n`Authorization: Bearer`); the Shard adds no sign-in of its own and relies on Vetro's. With pairing on, Vetro answers unpaired LAN requests with `401`;\nthat was seen on this TV, but a paired `notify` and the TV-side app (127.0.0.1) were not exercised. Please report if it behaves differently.\n\nNot tested: live TV and HDMI sources as the \"previous screen\", other TV models, other Tizen versions.\n","app/config.xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<widget xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets\" xmlns:tizen=\"http://tizen.org/ns/widgets\" id=\"http://localhost/notifcenter\" version=\"0.2.0\" viewmodes=\"maximized\">\n  <tizen:application id=\"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" package=\"NotifCtr01\" required_version=\"6.0\"/>\n  <name>Notification Center</name>\n  <icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n  <content src=\"index.html\"/>\n  <access origin=\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\" subdomains=\"false\"/>\n  <feature name=\"http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/internet\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/notification\"/>\n  <tizen:profile name=\"tv-samsung\"/>\n  <tizen:service id=\"NotifCtr01.Svc\" auto-restart=\"false\" on-boot=\"false\">\n    <tizen:content src=\"service.js\"/>\n    <tizen:name>Notification Center service</tizen:name>\n    <tizen:icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n    <tizen:description>Shows the Samsung notification banner without opening an app</tizen:description>\n  </tizen:service>\n</widget>\n","app/index.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Notification Center</title></head>\n<body style=\"background:#0f1218;color:#e8ecf2;font:28px sans-serif;margin:40px\">\n<div id=\"log\"></div>\n<script src=\"js/app.js\"></script>\n</body></html>\n","app/js/app.js":"(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASES = [\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\"];\n  var PATH = \"/plugins/notification-center/api/nt.js\";\n  var logEl = document.getElementById(\"log\"), i = 0;\n  function say(t) { var d = document.createElement(\"div\"); d.textContent = t; logEl.appendChild(d); }\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= BASES.length) { say(\"Could not load nt.js from the Shard. Is it running?\"); return; }\n    var s = document.createElement(\"script\");\n    s.src = BASES[i++] + PATH + \"?t=\" + new Date().getTime();\n    s.onerror = function () { say(\"nt.js failed: \" + s.src.split(\"?\")[0]); next(); };\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  })();\n})();\n","app/service.js":"// Background service of the Notification Center companion app (Node.js in the TV's web service runtime).\n// Vetro starts it (POST /apps/launch) each time a notification is queued in \"banner\" mode; it reads the Shard's queue and posts the native\n// Samsung banner with webapis.postPlainNotification, without opening any app.\n// The Shard is reached on the TV's own LAN address (found here), because loopback is not reachable from the service on every TV.\nvar HOSTS = ['127.0.0.1'];\ntry {\n  var ifs = require('os').networkInterfaces();\n  Object.keys(ifs).forEach(function (k) { ifs[k].forEach(function (i) { if (i.family === 'IPv4' && !i.internal && HOSTS.indexOf(i.address) < 0) { HOSTS.push(i.address); } }); });\n} catch (e) { /* keep loopback only */ }\nvar PATH = '/plugins/notification-center/api/notifications';\nvar seen = {};\nfunction check() {\n  var i = 0;\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= HOSTS.length) { return; }\n    fetch('http://' + HOSTS[i++] + ':8099' + PATH + '?t=' + Date.now()).then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error('http ' + r.status); } return r.json(); }).then(function (d) {\n      (d.notifications || []).forEach(function (n) {\n        if (seen[n.id]) { return; }\n        seen[n.id] = 1;\n        if (n.mode !== 'banner') { return; }   // \"full\" and \"both\" are shown by the companion app screen\n        try { webapis.postPlainNotification(n.title || 'Notification', n.message || '', parseInt(n.duration, 10) || 8); } catch (e) { /* API not available */ }\n      });\n    }).catch(function () { next(); });\n  })();\n}\nmodule.exports.onStart = check;\nmodule.exports.onRequest = check;\nmodule.exports.onStop = function () {};\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Notification Center: queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners\n// through a small companion web app (see README). It talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099 (to launch that app).\n// Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar http = require('http');\n\nvar MAX_TITLE = 40, MAX_MESSAGE = 200, MAX_QUEUE = 5, MAX_RECENT = 20, MAX_BODY = 8192;\nvar DEFAULT_SECONDS = 30, MIN_SECONDS = 5, MAX_SECONDS = 300, OPEN_EVERY_MS = 10000;\nvar DEFAULT_APP = 'NotifCtr01.NotifCenter';   // the companion app (screen: full-screen card, native banner)\nvar SERVICE_APP = 'NotifCtr01.Svc';           // its background service (native banner over the running app, no app switch)\nvar LEVELS = { info: 1, ok: 1, warn: 1, alert: 1 };\nvar MIN_DURATION = 1, MAX_DURATION = 60, DEFAULT_DURATION = 8;\nvar MODES = { both: 1, banner: 1, full: 1 };   // banner (default) = native banner over the running app, from the background service; full = full-screen card; both = card + banner\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var queue = [];      // active notifications (memory only)\n    var recent = [];     // last ones sent, for the page (memory only)\n    var seq = 0;\n    var lastOpen = 0;\n\n    // Display language of the app screen and the panel: 'en' (default) or 'pt'. The only thing kept in ctx.config.\n    function getLang() { var c = ctx.config.get() || {}; return c.lang === 'pt' ? 'pt' : 'en'; }\n    function appId() { return DEFAULT_APP; }   // fixed: nothing can point the Shard at another app\n    function send(res, code, type, body) {\n        res.writeHead(code, { 'Content-Type': type, 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(body);\n    }\n    function sendJson(res, code, obj) { send(res, code, 'application/json; charset=utf-8', JSON.stringify(obj)); }\n    // The companion app can read the queue as a <script> when the TV's web runtime blocks cross-origin XHR.\n    function sendScript(res, obj) {\n        var json = JSON.stringify(obj).replace(/</g, '\\\\u003c');\n        json = json.split(String.fromCharCode(0x2028)).join('\\\\u2028').split(String.fromCharCode(0x2029)).join('\\\\u2029');\n        send(res, 200, 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8', 'window.__ncNotes&&window.__ncNotes(' + json + ');');\n    }\n    function wantsScript(req) { return /[?&]js=1(&|$)/.test(String(req.url || '')); }\n    function readBody(req, cb) {\n        var s = '';\n        req.on('data', function (d) { s += d; if (s.length > MAX_BODY) { req.destroy(); } });\n        req.on('end', function () { cb(s); });\n    }\n    function clean(text, max) {\n        return String(text == null ? '' : text).replace(/[\\x00-\\x1f]/g, ' ').slice(0, max).trim();\n    }\n    function prune() {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        queue = queue.filter(function (n) { return n.expires > now; });\n    }\n\n    // Asks Vetro to launch the companion app (at most once every 10 s), or its background service (every time: it is\n    // headless, so launching it only makes it read the queue and post the banner).\n    function openApp(service) {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        if (!service) {\n            if (now - lastOpen < OPEN_EVERY_MS) { return 'skipped (less than 10 s since the last launch)'; }\n            lastOpen = now;\n        }\n        var body = JSON.stringify({ appId: service ? SERVICE_APP : appId() });\n        try {\n            var rq = http.request({\n                host: '127.0.0.1', port: 8099, path: '/apps/launch', method: 'POST', timeout: 5000,\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body) }\n            }, function (r) { r.resume(); });\n            rq.on('error', function () { /* Vetro busy or app not installed */ });\n            rq.on('timeout', function () { rq.destroy(); });\n            rq.write(body);\n            rq.end();\n            return 'requested';\n        } catch (e) { return 'error'; }\n    }\n\n    function handleNotify(req, res) {\n        readBody(req, function (raw) {\n            var b;\n            try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n            b = b || {};\n            var message = clean(b.message, MAX_MESSAGE);\n            if (!message) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'message is required' }); }\n            var secs = parseInt(b.seconds, 10);\n            if (!(secs >= MIN_SECONDS)) { secs = DEFAULT_SECONDS; }\n            if (secs > MAX_SECONDS) { secs = MAX_SECONDS; }\n            // duration = how long the notification stays on the TV screen (the app shows it, then returns to the previous app).\n            var dur = parseInt(b.duration, 10);\n            if (!(dur >= MIN_DURATION)) { dur = DEFAULT_DURATION; }\n            if (dur > MAX_DURATION) { dur = MAX_DURATION; }\n            if (secs < dur + 20) { secs = dur + 20; }\n            prune();\n            seq += 1;\n            var note = {\n                id: seq + '-' + Date.now().toString(36),\n                title: clean(b.title, MAX_TITLE),\n                message: message,\n                level: LEVELS[b.level] ? b.level : 'info',\n                mode: MODES[b.mode] ? b.mode : 'banner',\n                duration: dur,\n                expires: Date.now() + secs * 1000\n            };\n            queue.push(note);\n            if (queue.length > MAX_QUEUE) { queue.shift(); }\n            recent.unshift({ id: note.id, title: note.title, message: note.message, level: note.level, mode: note.mode, duration: note.duration, at: Date.now() });\n            if (recent.length > MAX_RECENT) { recent.pop(); }\n            var opened = b.open === false ? 'not requested' : openApp(note.mode === 'banner');\n            sendJson(res, 200, { ok: true, id: note.id, open: opened });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function sendFile(res, name, type) {\n        fs.readFile(path.join(__dirname, name), 'utf8', function (err, text) {\n            if (err) { return sendJson(res, 500, { error: name + ' is missing' }); }\n            send(res, 200, type, text);\n        });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {},\n        stop: function () { queue = []; recent = []; },\n        status: function () { prune(); return { queued: queue.length, appId: appId() }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            sub = String(sub || '').split('?')[0].replace(/^\\/+|\\/+$/g, '');\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'ui.html', 'text/html; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'nt.js' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'nt.js', 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notify' && req.method === 'POST') { handleNotify(req, res); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notifications' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                prune();\n                var now = Date.now();\n                var out = { lang: getLang(), notifications: queue.map(function (n) {\n                    return { id: n.id, title: n.title, message: n.message, level: n.level, mode: n.mode, duration: n.duration, seconds: Math.ceil((n.expires - now) / 1000) };\n                }) };\n                if (wantsScript(req)) { sendScript(res, out); } else { sendJson(res, 200, out); }\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'lang' && req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { lang: getLang() }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'lang' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readBody(req, function (raw) {\n                    var b;\n                    try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n                    if (!b || (b.lang !== 'en' && b.lang !== 'pt')) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'lang must be en or pt' }); }\n                    var c = ctx.config.get() || {};\n                    c.lang = b.lang;\n                    ctx.config.set(c);\n                    sendJson(res, 200, { lang: b.lang });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'recent' && req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { recent: recent }); return true; }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","nt.js":"// Logic of the companion web app, served by the Shard (the app on the TV is only a thin loader, see README).\n// It runs inside the app, with the app's `notification` privilege. Plain ES5.\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  if (window.__ncLoaded) { return; }\n  window.__ncLoaded = true;\n\n  var BASES = ['http://127.0.0.1:8099'];\n  // Also try the address this script was loaded from (the loader may have reached the Shard over the LAN).\n  try {\n    var me = document.currentScript && document.currentScript.src, o = me && /^(https?:\\/\\/[^\\/]+)\\/plugins\\//.exec(me);\n    if (o && BASES.indexOf(o[1]) < 0) { BASES.push(o[1]); }\n  } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n  var NOTES_PATH = '/plugins/notification-center/api/notifications';\n  var SEEN_KEY = 'nc_seen', WATCH_MS = 5000;\n  var logEl = document.getElementById('log');\n  var apiGood = null, busy = false;\n\n\n  // Screen shown while the app is open: a One UI style card (EN/PT by the TV language). The banner itself is the TV's native one.\n  // The language is a Shard setting (default English); it is applied as soon as the first answer from the Shard arrives.\n  var DICT = {\n    en: { wait: 'Notification Center', ready: 'Waiting for notifications', sent: 'Notification sent', back: 'Returning to the previous app in', err: 'Cannot reach the Shard' },\n    pt: { wait: 'Centro de Notifica\\u00E7\\u00F5es', ready: '\\u00C0 espera de avisos', sent: 'Aviso enviado', back: 'A voltar \\u00E0 aplica\\u00E7\\u00E3o anterior em', err: 'Sem liga\\u00E7\\u00E3o ao Shard' }\n  };\n  var TX = DICT.en;\n  var COL = { info: '#2f7bff', ok: '#2fc28b', warn: '#f5a524', alert: '#f0506e' };\n  // One UI style line icons (24x24, round caps): info, done, warning, alert.\n  var ICON_BODY = {\n    info: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 11v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    ok: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M7.6 12.6l3 3 5.8-6.4\"/>',\n    warn: '<path d=\"M12 3.8L21.2 20H2.8z\"/><path d=\"M12 10v4.6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17.4\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    alert: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 7v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"16.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>'\n  };\n  function iconSvg(level, size) {\n    return '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"' + size + '\" height=\"' + size + '\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">' + (ICON_BODY[level] || ICON_BODY.info) + '</svg>';\n  }\n  var cardEl = null;\n  (function buildUi() {\n    var st = document.createElement('style');\n    st.textContent = 'body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 30% 20%,#17203a,#07090f);color:#eef2f9;font-family:SamsungOne,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}' +\n      '#nc{position:fixed;left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);width:1100px;max-width:90%;text-align:center}' +\n      '#nc h1{font-size:44px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 8px}#nc p{font-size:28px;color:#8b96ab;margin:0 0 40px}' +\n      '#nc .card{display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:center;text-align:left;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:36px;padding:34px 42px;border-left:12px solid var(--c);margin-top:24px}' +\n      '#nc .ic{width:96px;height:96px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--c);display:grid;place-items:center;flex:none}' +\n      '#nc .t{font-size:38px;font-weight:600}#nc .m{font-size:30px;color:#c4cde0;margin-top:6px}#log{display:none}';\n    document.head.appendChild(st);\n    cardEl = document.createElement('div'); cardEl.id = 'nc';\n    cardEl.innerHTML = '<h1></h1><p></p><div id=\"ncl\"></div>';\n    document.body.appendChild(cardEl);\n    applyLang('en');\n  })();\n  function applyLang(l) {\n    TX = DICT[l] || DICT.en;\n    if (!cardEl) { return; }\n    cardEl.getElementsByTagName('h1')[0].textContent = '\\uD83D\\uDD14 ' + TX.wait;\n    if (!document.getElementById('ncl').firstChild) { cardEl.getElementsByTagName('p')[0].textContent = TX.ready; }\n  }\n  function showCard(n) {\n    if (!cardEl) { return; }\n    var c = COL[n.level] || COL.info, d = document.createElement('div');\n    d.className = 'card'; d.style.setProperty('--c', c);\n    var ic = document.createElement('div'); ic.className = 'ic'; ic.innerHTML = iconSvg(n.level, 56);\n    var b = document.createElement('div'), t = document.createElement('div'), m = document.createElement('div');\n    t.className = 't'; t.textContent = n.title || ''; m.className = 'm'; m.textContent = n.message || '';\n    b.appendChild(t); b.appendChild(m); d.appendChild(ic); d.appendChild(b);\n    var host = document.getElementById('ncl'); host.appendChild(d);\n    cardEl.getElementsByTagName('p')[0].textContent = TX.sent;\n  }\n\n  function now() { var d = new Date(); function p(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; } return p(d.getHours()) + ':' + p(d.getMinutes()) + ':' + p(d.getSeconds()); }\n  function log(cls, text) {\n    if (!logEl) { return; }\n    var line = document.createElement('div');\n    line.className = cls; line.textContent = now() + '  ' + text;\n    logEl.appendChild(line);\n    while (logEl.childNodes.length > 14) { logEl.removeChild(logEl.firstChild); }\n  }\n\n  function xhrGet(base, cb) {\n    var x = new XMLHttpRequest(), done = false;\n    function end(err, text) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(err, text); } }\n    try {\n      x.open('GET', base + NOTES_PATH); x.timeout = 4000;\n      x.onload = function () { if (x.status === 200) { end(null, x.responseText); } else { end('http ' + x.status); } };\n      x.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n      x.ontimeout = function () { end('timeout'); };\n      x.send();\n    } catch (e) { end('blocked'); }\n  }\n  function scriptGet(base, cb) {\n    var s = document.createElement('script'), done = false, t;\n    function end(err, data) {\n      if (done) { return; }\n      done = true; clearTimeout(t); window.__ncNotes = undefined;\n      if (s.parentNode) { s.parentNode.removeChild(s); }\n      cb(err, data);\n    }\n    window.__ncNotes = function (d) { end(null, d); };\n    s.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n    t = setTimeout(function () { end('timeout'); }, 5000);\n    s.src = base + NOTES_PATH + '?js=1&t=' + new Date().getTime();\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  }\n  function fetchQueue(done) {\n    var list = apiGood ? [apiGood] : BASES, i = 0, errors = [];\n    (function next() {\n      if (i >= list.length) { return done(errors.join('; ') || 'no address'); }\n      var base = list[i++];\n      xhrGet(base, function (err, text) {\n        if (!err) { try { apiGood = base; var jd = JSON.parse(text); applyLang(jd.lang); return done(null, jd.notifications || []); } catch (e) { err = 'json'; } }\n        scriptGet(base, function (err2, data) {\n          if (!err2) { apiGood = base; applyLang(data && data.lang); return done(null, (data && data.notifications) || []); }\n          errors.push(base + ' xhr:' + err + ' script:' + err2); next();\n        });\n      });\n    })();\n  }\n\n  function post(title, body, cb) {\n    try {\n      if (!window.Notification) { return cb('window.Notification is missing'); }\n      var show = function () { try { new Notification(title, { body: body }); cb(null); } catch (e) { cb('new Notification: ' + e.message); } };\n      if (Notification.permission === 'granted') { return show(); }\n      var r = Notification.requestPermission(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } });\n      if (r && r.then) { r.then(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } }); }\n    } catch (e) { cb(e.message); }\n  }\n\n  var cdTimer = null;\n  function countdown(sec) {\n    if (!cardEl || cdTimer) { return; }\n    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    el.style.cssText = 'margin-top:48px;color:#8b96ab;font-size:34px';\n    cardEl.appendChild(el);\n    (function tick() {\n      el.innerHTML = '';\n      var lbl = document.createElement('div'), num = document.createElement('div');\n      lbl.textContent = TX.back;\n      num.textContent = String(sec);\n      num.style.cssText = 'font-size:220px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.05;color:#fff';\n      el.appendChild(lbl); el.appendChild(num);\n      if (sec <= 0) { return; }\n      sec -= 1; cdTimer = setTimeout(tick, 1000);\n    })();\n  }\n\n  // On start, on resume and every few seconds while visible: post what is new, stay open while the banner shows, then exit.\n  function check(why) {\n    if (busy) { return; }\n    busy = true;\n    fetchQueue(function (err, list) {\n      if (err) { busy = false; return log('err', why + ': Shard unreachable (' + err + ')'); }\n      var seen = {}; try { seen = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SEEN_KEY) || '{}'); } catch (e) { seen = {}; }\n      var fresh = list.filter(function (n) { return !seen[n.id]; });\n      if (!fresh.length) { busy = false; return log('inf', why + ': nothing new'); }\n      var pending = fresh.length;\n      // mode: 'banner' = native Samsung banner only, 'full' = full-screen card only, anything else = both.\n      // How long to stay on screen: the longest duration asked (default 8 s), exactly as requested.\n      var stayMs = 0;\n      fresh.forEach(function (n) { var d = parseInt(n.duration, 10) || 8; if (d * 1000 > stayMs) { stayMs = d * 1000; } });\n      var onlyBanner = fresh.every(function (n) { return n.mode === 'banner'; });\n      if (cardEl) { cardEl.style.display = onlyBanner ? 'none' : ''; }\n      fresh.forEach(function (n) {\n        seen[n.id] = 1;\n        if (n.mode !== 'banner') { showCard(n); }\n        (n.mode === 'full' ? function (t, b, cb) { cb(null); } : post)(n.title || 'Notification', n.message || '', function (e) {\n          log(e ? 'err' : 'ok', (n.title || 'Notification') + ': ' + (e || 'posted'));\n          pending -= 1;\n          if (pending) { return; }\n          try { localStorage.setItem(SEEN_KEY, JSON.stringify(seen)); } catch (x) { /* storage unavailable */ }\n          busy = false; countdown(Math.round(stayMs / 1000));\n          // Leaving too early hides the banner: stay open while it is on screen.\n          setTimeout(function () { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }, stayMs);\n        });\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  check('start');\n  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () { if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') { check('resume'); } });\n  setInterval(function () { if (document.visibilityState !== 'hidden') { check('watch'); } }, WATCH_MS);\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {\n    if (e.keyCode === 10009 || e.keyCode === 27) { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }\n  });\n})();\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark light\">\n<title>Notification Center</title>\n<style>\n:root { --bg: #0b0e14; --card: #161b26; --line: #262e3f; --txt: #eef2f9; --dim: #8b96ab; --acc: #2f7bff; --info: #2f7bff; --ok: #2fc28b; --warn: #f5a524; --alert: #f0506e; }\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 16px; font: 15px/1.45 \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--txt); }\n.head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 14px; }\n.logo { width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2f7bff, #7b5cff); display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 22px; }\nh1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0; flex: 1; font-weight: 600; }\n.lang { display: flex; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; }\n.lang button { border: 0; background: none; color: var(--dim); padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; font: inherit; }\n.lang button.on { background: var(--acc); color: #fff; }\n.grid { display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); }\n.card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; padding: 16px; }\nh2 { font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 12px; font-weight: 600; }\ninput, button { font: inherit; color: inherit; }\ninput[type=text], input[type=number] { width: 100%; background: #0f131c; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\ninput:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--acc); border-color: transparent; }\n.row { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.row label { color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }\n.row input[type=number] { width: 80px; margin: 0; }\n.dur { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; width: 100%; color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; }\n.dur input { flex: 1; accent-color: var(--acc); margin: 0; }\n.dur b { color: var(--txt); min-width: 44px; text-align: right; font-weight: 600; }\n.wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n.levels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n.lv { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #0f131c; border-radius: 14px; padding: 10px 4px; cursor: pointer; text-align: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); }\n.lv i { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; margin: 0 auto 6px; }\n.lv.on { color: #fff; border-color: var(--c); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--c); }\n.modes { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n.md { flex: 1; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #0f131c; border-radius: 20px; padding: 8px 6px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--dim); font-size: 12px; }\n.md.on { color: #fff; border-color: var(--acc); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--acc); }\n.rs { margin: 0 0 0 auto; padding: 4px 12px; font-size: 12px; flex: none; }\n.send { margin-left: auto; background: var(--acc); border: 0; border-radius: 22px; padding: 10px 26px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; }\n.send:active { transform: scale(.97); }\n.msg { min-height: 20px; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); } .ok { color: var(--ok); } .err { color: var(--alert); }\n.scene { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: #0a1120; }\n@keyframes ncSlide { 0% { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(90px); } 14%, 84% { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); } 100% { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(90px); } }\n@keyframes ncFade { 0%, 4% { opacity: 0; } 14%, 84% { opacity: 1; } 96%, 100% { opacity: 0; } }\n.sc-banner { animation: ncSlide 6s ease-in-out infinite; }\n.sc-card { animation: ncFade 6s ease-in-out infinite; }\n.prev { background: #0f131c; border-radius: 16px; padding: 14px; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; border-left: 5px solid var(--c, var(--info)); }\n.prev .ic { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--c, var(--info)); display: grid; place-items: center; flex: none; }\n.prev b { display: block; } .prev span { color: var(--dim); font-size: 14px; word-break: break-word; }\nul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\nli { display: flex; gap: 10px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); align-items: flex-start; }\nli:last-child { border: 0; }\nli .dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 6px; flex: none; background: var(--c); }\nli small { color: var(--dim); display: block; }\n.ghost { background: none; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; padding: 6px 14px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--dim); margin-top: 10px; }\n.empty { color: var(--dim); text-align: center; padding: 18px 0; }\npre { background: #0f131c; border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px; font-size: 12px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; margin: 0; color: #b9c4dc; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"head\">\n  <div class=\"logo\">&#128276;</div>\n  <h1 data-t=\"title\">Notification Center</h1>\n  <div class=\"lang\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"l-en\">EN</button><button type=\"button\" id=\"l-pt\">PT</button></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"send\">Send a notification</h2>\n    <div class=\"levels\" id=\"levels\"></div>\n    <div class=\"modes\" id=\"modes\"></div>\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"title\" maxlength=\"40\" data-p=\"ph_title\">\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"message\" maxlength=\"200\" data-p=\"ph_msg\">\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <div class=\"dur\"><span data-t=\"secs\">Show for (s)</span><input type=\"range\" id=\"secs\" min=\"1\" max=\"60\" value=\"8\"><b id=\"secsv\">8 s</b></div>\n      <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"open\" checked> <span data-t=\"open\">Show on TV now</span></label>\n      <button class=\"send\" id=\"send\" type=\"button\" data-t=\"btn\">Send</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"msg\" id=\"result\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"preview\">Preview</h2>\n    <svg id=\"scene\" class=\"scene\" viewBox=\"0 0 1920 1080\" role=\"img\" font-family=\"SamsungOneUI, system-ui, Segoe UI, sans-serif\" font-weight=\"500\">\n      <defs>\n        <linearGradient id=\"tvSky\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#101c3f\"/><stop offset=\".45\" stop-color=\"#553b73\"/><stop offset=\".72\" stop-color=\"#d9707a\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#f6b26b\"/></linearGradient>\n        <radialGradient id=\"tvSun\" cx=\".5\" cy=\".5\" r=\".5\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#fff2cf\" stop-opacity=\".95\"/><stop offset=\".35\" stop-color=\"#ffc58a\" stop-opacity=\".5\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#ffc58a\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/></radialGradient>\n        <linearGradient id=\"tvWater\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#f0a26c\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#1a2547\"/></linearGradient>\n      </defs>\n      <rect width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" fill=\"url(#tvSky)\"/><circle cx=\"1330\" cy=\"640\" r=\"420\" fill=\"url(#tvSun)\"/><circle cx=\"1330\" cy=\"640\" r=\"64\" fill=\"#fff0c9\"/>\n      <path d=\"M0 690 220 520 420 640 640 470 880 650 1080 560 1290 690 1500 540 1740 660 1920 590V760H0z\" fill=\"#42375f\"/>\n      <path d=\"M0 760 180 640 400 740 640 620 900 760 1160 650 1420 770 1680 670 1920 740V800H0z\" fill=\"#26274a\"/>\n      <rect y=\"780\" width=\"1920\" height=\"300\" fill=\"url(#tvWater)\"/>\n      <rect x=\"1250\" y=\"790\" width=\"160\" height=\"6\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffe3b3\" opacity=\".7\"/><rect x=\"1280\" y=\"820\" width=\"100\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffe3b3\" opacity=\".45\"/><rect x=\"1300\" y=\"850\" width=\"60\" height=\"4\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffe3b3\" opacity=\".3\"/>\n      <path d=\"M0 900 0 1080H1920V920C1700 880 1500 930 1250 900 900 860 600 930 0 900z\" fill=\"#0d1530\" opacity=\".55\"/>\n      <g id=\"dyn\"></g>\n    </svg>\n    <div class=\"msg\" data-t=\"prevnote\">The TV shows its own native banner; this is only an approximation.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"recent\">Recently sent</h2>\n    <ul id=\"recent\"></ul>\n    <button class=\"ghost\" id=\"refresh\" type=\"button\" data-t=\"refresh\">Refresh</button>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card wide\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"app\">Companion app</h2>\n    <div class=\"msg\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px\" data-t=\"appnote\">Launches NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (fixed id). It must be installed on the TV, see the README.</div>\n    <h2 data-t=\"curl\">Send from another device</h2>\n    <pre id=\"curl\"></pre>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };\n  var T = {\n    en: { title: \"Notification Center\", send: \"Send a notification\", secs: \"Show for (s)\", open: \"Show on TV now\", btn: \"Send\", preview: \"Preview\",\n      prevnote: \"The TV shows its own native banner; this is only an approximation.\", recent: \"Recently sent\", refresh: \"Refresh\", app: \"Companion app\",\n      appnote: \"Launches NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (fixed id). It must be installed on the TV, see the README.\", curl: \"Send from another device\",\n      ph_title: \"Title (optional)\", ph_msg: \"Message\", sending: \"Sending...\", queued: \"Sent to the TV\", queuedq: \"Queued (TV not launched)\", none: \"Nothing sent yet.\", notitle: \"Notification\",\n      info: \"Info\", ok: \"Done\", warn: \"Warning\", alert: \"Alert\", sample: \"Your message appears here\", back: \"Returning to the previous app in\",\n      mode: \"Show as\", m_both: \"Both\", m_banner: \"Samsung banner\", m_full: \"Full screen\", resend: \"Resend\", resent: \"Sent again\" },\n    pt: { title: \"Centro de Notifica\\u00E7\\u00F5es\", send: \"Enviar notifica\\u00E7\\u00E3o\", secs: \"Mostrar durante (s)\", open: \"Mostrar na TV agora\", btn: \"Enviar\", preview: \"Pr\\u00E9-visualiza\\u00E7\\u00E3o\",\n      prevnote: \"A TV mostra o seu pr\\u00F3prio aviso nativo; isto \\u00E9 s\\u00F3 uma aproxima\\u00E7\\u00E3o.\", recent: \"Enviadas recentemente\", refresh: \"Atualizar\", app: \"App companheira\",\n      appnote: \"Lan\\u00E7a NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (id fixo). Tem de estar instalada na TV, ver o README.\", curl: \"Enviar a partir de outro dispositivo\",\n      ph_title: \"T\\u00EDtulo (opcional)\", ph_msg: \"Mensagem\", sending: \"A enviar...\", queued: \"Enviada para a TV\", queuedq: \"Em fila (TV n\\u00E3o lan\\u00E7ada)\", none: \"Ainda nada enviado.\", notitle: \"Notifica\\u00E7\\u00E3o\",\n      info: \"Info\", ok: \"Conclu\\u00EDdo\", warn: \"Aviso\", alert: \"Alerta\", sample: \"A sua mensagem aparece aqui\", back: \"A voltar \\u00E0 aplica\\u00E7\\u00E3o anterior em\",\n      mode: \"Mostrar como\", m_both: \"Ambos\", m_banner: \"Aviso Samsung\", m_full: \"Ecr\\u00E3 inteiro\", resend: \"Reenviar\", resent: \"Enviada de novo\" }\n  };\n  var LEVELS = [\"info\", \"ok\", \"warn\", \"alert\"];\n  // One UI style line icons (24x24, round caps): info, done, warning, alert.\n  var ICON_BODY = {\n    info: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 11v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    ok: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M7.6 12.6l3 3 5.8-6.4\"/>',\n    warn: '<path d=\"M12 3.8L21.2 20H2.8z\"/><path d=\"M12 10v4.6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17.4\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    alert: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 7v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"16.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>'\n  };\n  function iconSvg(level, size) {\n    return '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"' + size + '\" height=\"' + size + '\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">' + (ICON_BODY[level] || ICON_BODY.info) + '</svg>';\n  }\n  var COLORS = { info: \"#2f7bff\", ok: \"#2fc28b\", warn: \"#f5a524\", alert: \"#f0506e\" };\n  var lang = \"en\", level = \"info\", mode = \"banner\", lastRecent = [];\n  function tr(k) { return T[lang][k] || T.en[k] || k; }\n  function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? \"\" : s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, function (c) { return { \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\", \"'\": \"&#39;\" }[c]; }); }\n  function say(text, cls) { $(\"result\").textContent = text || \"\"; $(\"result\").className = \"msg \" + (cls || \"\"); }\n  function api(path, body) {\n    var opt = body ? { method: \"POST\", headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" }, body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {};\n    return fetch(path, opt).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error(j.error || \"error \" + r.status); } return j; }); });\n  }\n  function icon(l) { return iconSvg(l, 24); }\n  function paintLevels() {\n    $(\"levels\").innerHTML = LEVELS.map(function (l) {\n      return '<button type=\"button\" class=\"lv' + (l === level ? \" on\" : \"\") + '\" data-l=\"' + l + '\" style=\"--c:' + COLORS[l] + '\"><i style=\"background:' + COLORS[l] + '\">' + iconSvg(l, 22) + \"</i>\" + esc(tr(l)) + \"</button>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    var b = $(\"levels\").getElementsByTagName(\"button\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < b.length; i++) { b[i].addEventListener(\"click\", function () { level = this.getAttribute(\"data-l\"); paintLevels(); preview(); }); }\n  }\n  function paintModes() {\n    var MODES = [\"banner\", \"full\", \"both\"];\n    $(\"modes\").innerHTML = MODES.map(function (m) {\n      return '<button type=\"button\" class=\"md' + (m === mode ? \" on\" : \"\") + '\" data-m=\"' + m + '\">' + esc(tr(\"m_\" + m)) + \"</button>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    var b = $(\"modes\").getElementsByTagName(\"button\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < b.length; i++) { b[i].addEventListener(\"click\", function () { mode = this.getAttribute(\"data-m\"); paintModes(); preview(); }); }\n  }\n  function cut(t, n) { t = String(t || \"\"); return t.length > n ? t.slice(0, n - 1) + \"\\u2026\" : t; }\n  function iconAt(l, x, y, size) {\n    return '<svg x=\"' + x + '\" y=\"' + y + '\" width=\"' + size + '\" height=\"' + size + '\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">' + (ICON_BODY[l] || ICON_BODY.info) + \"</svg>\";\n  }\n  // Preview drawn like the Vetro UI overview: the same sunset scene as the TV, with the notification on top.\n  function preview() {\n    var c = COLORS[level], ttl = $(\"title\").value || tr(\"notitle\"), msg = $(\"message\").value || tr(\"sample\");\n    var dur = parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 8, h = \"\";\n    if (mode !== \"banner\") {\n      h += '<g class=\"sc-card\"><rect width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" fill=\"#07090f\" fill-opacity=\".55\"/>' +\n        '<rect x=\"360\" y=\"330\" width=\"1200\" height=\"310\" rx=\"64\" fill=\"#fff\" fill-opacity=\".1\"/><rect x=\"360\" y=\"330\" width=\"18\" height=\"310\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"' + c + '\"/>' +\n        '<circle cx=\"520\" cy=\"485\" r=\"74\" fill=\"' + c + '\"/>' + iconAt(level, 520 - 44, 485 - 44, 88) +\n        '<text x=\"640\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"54\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#fff\">' + esc(cut(ttl, 30)) + '</text>' +\n        '<text x=\"640\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"38\" fill=\"#c4cde0\">' + esc(cut(msg, 52)) + \"</text>\" +\n        '<text x=\"960\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#8b96ab\">' + esc(tr(\"back\")) + '</text>' +\n        '<text x=\"960\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"160\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#fff\">' + dur + \"</text></g>\";\n    }\n    if (mode !== \"full\") {\n      h += '<g class=\"sc-banner\"><rect x=\"1236\" y=\"60\" width=\"628\" height=\"196\" rx=\"44\" fill=\"#fff\" fill-opacity=\".22\"/><rect x=\"1238\" y=\"62\" width=\"624\" height=\"192\" rx=\"42\" fill=\"#243448\" fill-opacity=\".94\"/>' +\n        '<circle cx=\"1312\" cy=\"140\" r=\"44\" fill=\"' + c + '\"/>' + iconAt(level, 1312 - 27, 140 - 27, 54) +\n        '<text x=\"1380\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#fff\">' + esc(cut(ttl, 22)) + \"</text>\" +\n        '<text x=\"1380\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" fill-opacity=\".75\">' + esc(cut(msg, 30)) + \"</text>\" +\n        '<text x=\"1380\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8fbaff\">OK</text><text x=\"1470\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#8fbaff\">View history</text></g>';\n    }\n    $(\"dyn\").innerHTML = h;\n  }\n\n  function recent() {\n    api(\"recent\").then(function (d) {\n      lastRecent = d.recent;\n      $(\"recent\").innerHTML = d.recent.length ? d.recent.map(function (n, i) {\n        return '<li style=\"--c:' + (COLORS[n.level] || COLORS.info) + '\"><span class=\"dot\"></span><div><b>' + esc(n.title || tr(\"notitle\")) + \"</b> \" + esc(n.message) +\n          \"<small>\" + new Date(n.at).toLocaleTimeString() + \"</small></div>\" +\n          '<button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost rs\" data-i=\"' + i + '\">' + esc(tr(\"resend\")) + \"</button></li>\";\n      }).join(\"\") : '<li class=\"empty\">' + esc(tr(\"none\")) + \"</li>\";\n      var rb = $(\"recent\").getElementsByClassName(\"rs\"), k;\n      for (k = 0; k < rb.length; k++) {\n        rb[k].addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n          var n = lastRecent[parseInt(this.getAttribute(\"data-i\"), 10)];\n          if (!n) { return; }\n          api(\"notify\", { title: n.title, message: n.message, level: n.level, mode: n.mode, duration: parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 8, open: $(\"open\").checked })\n            .then(function () { say(tr(\"resent\"), \"ok\"); recent(); })\n            .catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n        });\n      }\n    }).catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n  }\n  function applyLang() {\n    document.documentElement.lang = lang;\n    var els = document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-t]\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < els.length; i++) { els[i].textContent = tr(els[i].getAttribute(\"data-t\")); }\n    els = document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-p]\");\n    for (i = 0; i < els.length; i++) { els[i].placeholder = tr(els[i].getAttribute(\"data-p\")); }\n    $(\"l-en\").className = lang === \"en\" ? \"on\" : \"\"; $(\"l-pt\").className = lang === \"pt\" ? \"on\" : \"\";\n    paintLevels(); paintModes(); preview(); recent();\n  }\n  // The language is a Shard setting (default English); it also decides the language of the app screen on the TV.\n  function setLang(l) { lang = l; applyLang(); api(\"lang\", { lang: l }).catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); }); }\n  // The dashboard frame has no allow-forms: use buttons and the Enter key, not <form>.\n  $(\"send\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    say(tr(\"sending\"));\n    api(\"notify\", { title: $(\"title\").value, message: $(\"message\").value, level: level, mode: mode, duration: parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 8, open: $(\"open\").checked })\n      .then(function (r) { say(r.open === \"not requested\" ? tr(\"queuedq\") : tr(\"queued\"), \"ok\"); $(\"message\").value = \"\"; preview(); recent(); })\n      .catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n  });\n  $(\"message\").addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) { if (e.key === \"Enter\") { $(\"send\").click(); } });\n  $(\"message\").addEventListener(\"input\", preview); $(\"title\").addEventListener(\"input\", preview);\n  $(\"secs\").addEventListener(\"input\", function () { $(\"secsv\").textContent = this.value + \" s\"; preview(); });\n  $(\"refresh\").addEventListener(\"click\", recent);\n  $(\"l-en\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () { setLang(\"en\"); });\n  $(\"l-pt\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () { setLang(\"pt\"); });\n  $(\"curl\").textContent = 'curl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\\\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\\\\n  -d \\'{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"level\":\"ok\",\"seconds\":30}\\'';\n  applyLang();\n  api(\"lang\").then(function (d) { if (T[d.lang] && d.lang !== lang) { lang = d.lang; applyLang(); } }).catch(function () { /* keep English */ });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}
